275
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:51,780
Just say the word and I will.

276
00:12:52,780 --> 00:12:53,660
Nah, son.

277
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,520
You're ashamed to waste those locks.

278
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:56,740
Why not just tie it in the back?

279
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:57,920
Please, Miyamoto.

280
00:12:58,420 --> 00:12:59,280
Ignore him.

281
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:00,820
You mean like this?

282
00:13:01,320 --> 00:13:02,820
Hey, get us some bobby pins.

283
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:03,460
Ugh.

284
00:13:04,920 --> 00:13:05,440
Fine.

285
00:13:06,420 --> 00:13:07,680
You're a handsome kid.

286
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,200
I'm sure a guy like you gets all the girls.

287
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:12,560
I'm kind of the opposite, sir.

288
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,720
Are you really okay with settling for Kyoko?

289
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:17,640
Yeah, I am.

290
00:13:18,040 --> 00:13:19,240
But I'm not settling.

291
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:20,620
I fell for her.

292
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:22,620
What a charmer!

293
00:13:22,800 --> 00:13:24,520
I wish I could go back to high school.

294
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:28,000
Here, I got your bobby pins.

295
00:13:28,620 --> 00:13:32,140
Now that I think about it, you're exactly like Yoriko was at that age.

296
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:35,520
And something tells me you've been an immature loser your entire life.

297
00:13:39,520 --> 00:13:40,620
Hi, Kiyosuke.

298
00:13:46,900 --> 00:13:47,460
No.

299
00:13:48,540 --> 00:13:50,020
Oh, it's terrible!

300
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:53,920
You're here in time for dinner, but I don't have enough to feed you.

301
00:13:54,160 --> 00:13:55,260
You're joking, right?

302
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:59,000
There's me, Sota, then Kyoko and Izumi, too.

303
00:13:59,100 --> 00:14:01,280
Hey, I can solve the problem by going home.

304
00:14:01,280 --> 00:14:02,540
That's silly.

305
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,580
Kiyosuke doesn't even have silverware.

306
00:14:04,860 --> 00:14:06,300
I don't have silverware anymore!

307
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:08,820
We have takeout chopsticks you can use.

308
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,640
I don't have chopsticks either!

309
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:15,940
I should apologize for how annoying Kiyosuke was.

310
00:14:17,020 --> 00:14:17,760
It's okay.

311
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:18,860
You're too nice.

312
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,960
I know firsthand how pushy he can be.

313
00:14:23,240 --> 00:14:26,540
Somehow him being a hori kind of justifies his behavior.

314
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,520
Miyamura?

315
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:37,660
Something on your mind?

316
00:14:37,660 --> 00:14:38,160
Yeah.

317
00:14:38,160 --> 00:15:01,800
So listen, hori, when it comes to knowing the real you, I feel like I've barely scratched the surface.

318
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:07,020
But if you'll let me, I'd like to learn everything, little by little.

319
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:10,060
At least that's the hope I have.

320
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,460
Well, the feeling's mutual.

321
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:15,520
It is?

322
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:16,580
Yeah.

323
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:19,880
I can make it from here.

324
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:21,040
Okay.

325
00:15:21,700 --> 00:15:22,320
Be careful.

326
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,520
I'll, uh, see you tomorrow.

327
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,360
Hori!

328
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:29,820
Thank you.

329
00:15:31,960 --> 00:15:32,940
You're welcome?

330
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:54,160
Now I know how hard it is to say, see you tomorrow.

331
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:57,500
And just how fast your heart can beat.

332
00:15:57,500 --> 00:16:03,480
Yeah, so how many problems did we have for math again?

333
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:05,420
Huh?

334
00:16:06,540 --> 00:16:07,740
Oh, wow.

335
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:10,320
Yeah, of course.

336
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:13,060
Don't be stupid.

337
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:14,840
I'm the one who called you, remember?

338
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:16,860
Seriously, don't stress.

339
00:16:17,540 --> 00:16:18,260
You made it happen.

340
00:16:18,820 --> 00:16:19,320
That's awesome.

341
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:20,700
I'm cool with it.

342
00:16:21,500 --> 00:16:21,780
Yeah.

343
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,420
I'll see you at school.

344
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:23,520
Okay.

345
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:35,880
Oh, crap.

346
00:16:38,120 --> 00:16:39,400
So lame.

347
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:42,440
I was the one closest to her.

348
00:16:43,180 --> 00:16:44,200
The actual hell.

349
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,500
This sucks.

350
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:52,000
Maybe I'll get a part-time job.

351
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,520
Ooh, apply where I work.

352
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:02,980
For some reason, he seems kind of down.

353
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,340
There you are.

354
00:17:04,860 --> 00:17:05,140
Sakura?

355
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:06,740
Hello?

356
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:07,320
Oh!

357
00:17:08,340 --> 00:17:10,460
It's not like you to be a space case.

358
00:17:10,620 --> 00:17:12,200
I don't know what you're talking about.

359
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:13,680
I'm as down-to-earth as ever.

360
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:16,600
Let's head for the council room, okay?

361
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:18,880
What was out that window?

362
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:20,000
Nothing.

363
00:17:20,780 --> 00:17:21,660
Just drop it.

364
00:17:21,660 --> 00:17:22,100
Yeah, right.

365
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:23,820
Remy can tell your eyes were occupied.

366
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:25,780
I promise you they weren't.

367
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,240
So let's get going already.

368
00:17:27,920 --> 00:17:28,500
Come on!

369
00:17:29,640 --> 00:17:31,520
Is it something you need to hide from me?

370
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:35,620
Lately, you've been acting really weird.

371
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:36,840
That's not true.

372
00:17:37,740 --> 00:17:38,140
Yeah-ha!

373
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:39,820
Just now you zoned out.

374
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,380
So what's going on with you?

375
00:17:42,240 --> 00:17:43,440
Remy is willing to listen.

376
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:44,360
No judgment.

377
00:17:44,360 --> 00:17:50,820
Such big eyes.

378
00:17:50,820 --> 00:17:53,960
And her slender figure is the same as Hoodie's.

379
00:17:54,340 --> 00:17:55,960
I'm sure that's Ishikawa's type.

380
00:17:56,520 --> 00:17:58,360
Someone both pretty and cute.

381
00:17:58,360 --> 00:18:01,120
You wouldn't understand.

382
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,640
What would make you say that?

383
00:18:04,120 --> 00:18:05,860
You think I'm too stupid or something?

384
00:18:06,020 --> 00:18:06,580
Is that why?

385
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:07,080
No!

386
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:08,800
Of course not.

387
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:10,360
It's because...

388
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:13,100
How can you empathize when you look as cute as you do?

389
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:15,440
You don't know what it's like to be me!

390
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,060
What the hell?

391
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:21,640
Remy is genuinely concerned about you!

392
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,580
And I genuinely meant what I said!

393
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,320
I wish...

394
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:27,520
Things were different.

395
00:18:28,860 --> 00:18:30,100
In fact...

396
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:31,440
I wish I could be you!

397
00:18:36,600 --> 00:18:39,940
I'm as ugly on the inside as I am on the outside.

398
00:18:40,940 --> 00:18:41,820
How pitiful.

399
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:46,020
Why is somebody as hot as Ayasaki always hanging around Kono?

400
00:18:46,020 --> 00:18:47,860
They're like Beauty and the Beast!

401
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:50,060
I know I'll never be a beauty.

402
00:18:50,060 --> 00:18:51,900
Sakura!

403
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,020
What a cute name!

404
00:18:54,260 --> 00:18:55,160
I like it!

405
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:58,720
That's right.

406
00:18:59,180 --> 00:19:00,200
I don't need to be.

407
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:02,560
Because the beauty is my best friend.

408
00:19:16,440 --> 00:19:17,320
Feeling better?

409
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:18,440
Oh.

410
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:20,000
I went to the bathroom.

411
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,040
Guess you're still uneasy, huh?

412
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:26,180
Okay.

413
00:19:26,640 --> 00:19:26,920
So...

414
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:29,960
You know how you said I've been acting weird?

415
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:31,920
There's this...

416
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:33,260
Guy I like.

417
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:36,300
But the thing is, I'm not attractive like you are.

418
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:39,060
And I'm painfully aware of that fact.

419
00:19:39,780 --> 00:19:40,520
I...

420
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,260
Don't know.

421
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,700
I've never seen you blush before!

422
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:43,320
Hmm?

423
00:19:43,320 --> 00:19:49,440
I mean, you're always so calm and level-headed, so you don't often lose your composure, but...

424
00:19:49,440 --> 00:19:51,840
A little color in your cheeks makes you look cute.

425
00:19:51,840 --> 00:19:59,740
Thank you, Remy.

426
00:20:02,020 --> 00:20:02,460
What?

427
00:20:02,600 --> 00:20:04,200
You need me to hold your hand or something?

428
00:20:04,340 --> 00:20:06,780
No, but it'll only take a sec.

429
00:20:07,780 --> 00:20:07,980
Huh?

430
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:08,200
Huh?

431
00:20:08,200 --> 00:20:10,140
Hold up.

432
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:11,880
What are you two still doing here?

433
00:20:12,220 --> 00:20:13,280
I forgot something.

434
00:20:13,900 --> 00:20:14,740
Same with you?

435
00:20:14,960 --> 00:20:15,460
I didn't.

436
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:16,700
I'm just doing she was solid.

437
00:20:17,220 --> 00:20:20,280
Since you're here, Hori, I have a question about the English midterm.

438
00:20:20,280 --> 00:20:21,160
What?

439
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,660
How do I conjugate that one grammar form again?

440
00:20:23,740 --> 00:20:24,440
Try to remember.

441
00:20:24,740 --> 00:20:26,740
Don't tell me that you're feeling awkward, dude.

442
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:30,100
Maybe a little.

443
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:31,680
I'm so sorry.

444
00:20:32,600 --> 00:20:34,580
Didn't I tell you not to stress about this?

445
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:37,160
Hit it through your thick skull, moron.

446
00:20:42,520 --> 00:20:43,400
That's so funny.

447
00:20:43,420 --> 00:20:43,640
Ow!

448
00:20:44,260 --> 00:20:45,660
Jeez, you guys, get a room.

449
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:47,260
Gross.

450
00:20:47,260 --> 00:20:50,280
Are you serious with this answer right now?

451
00:20:50,640 --> 00:20:52,260
I swear you're worse than Iyorta.

452
00:20:52,920 --> 00:20:57,120
Unless it's a verb ending in I-N-G, I'm most likely going to screw it up.

453
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:58,760
Five o'clock already?

454
00:20:59,300 --> 00:21:00,140
Is that bad?

455
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,140
No, just expecting a guest.

456
00:21:03,480 --> 00:21:03,800
Izumi.

457
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:04,880
What's up?

458
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:13,480
What?

459
00:21:14,080 --> 00:21:15,920
I didn't mean you, Miyamura.

460
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,580
That's pretty hilarious, though.

461
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,300
Wait, but you said...

462
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:21,480
I meant Sota's friend.

463
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:22,920
His last name is Izumi.

464
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:24,540
Ah, gotcha.

465
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:28,520
And here I thought you were going to start calling me by my first name.

466
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:29,440
So what?

467
00:21:29,820 --> 00:21:30,780
Is that what you want?

468
00:21:31,600 --> 00:21:31,920
Yeah.

469
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:35,400
Kinda.

470
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:40,220
Why is it any time you get flustered now, I feel it twice as much?

471
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,680
Guess I didn't realize.

472
00:21:42,440 --> 00:21:42,980
My bad.

473
00:21:46,220 --> 00:21:46,700
Dummy.

474
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:48,780
Dummy Izumi.

475
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:56,720
You know, I like the sound of that.

476
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,720
But maybe next time try it without the dummy.

477
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:03,440
We're here!

478
00:22:03,440 --> 00:22:05,940
Why do you always have to open your big door mouth?

479
00:22:06,180 --> 00:22:07,460
Sounds like they're at it again.

480
00:22:07,460 --> 00:22:08,140
What's this, normal?

481
00:22:08,900 --> 00:22:10,420
Your family might need some help.

482
00:22:10,420 --> 00:22:12,320
I mean it, you dummy, dummy, dummy!

483
00:22:12,320 --> 00:22:42,300
There we go.

484
00:22:42,640 --> 00:22:49,280
now

485
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,800
you

486
00:23:12,320 --> 00:23:18,180
I'maccordo.

487
00:23:18,200 --> 00:23:24,840
I'm not guarantees because I remember that.

488
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:30,480
I'miverse pleading like Yiseliya,

489
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:36,940
No but it's not personal but if I Hokuto�� Weiseliya.

490
00:23:42,320 --> 00:23:44,320
You

